const body = `**Booking-domain verification lifecycle — built.** Branch \`feature/booking-domain-verify\` (off \`origin/integration/nexis-all\`), pushed to origin. Server .215 (nexis-app). tsc clean, \`npm run build\` passes in the worktree. NOT merged/deployed; no certbot/nginx touched on the live box.

**What shipped**
- State machine \`src/lib/domain.ts\`: PENDING -> VERIFYING -> LIVE / FAILED (back-compat with legacy PENDING_DNS/ERROR). site-url.ts still only trusts LIVE; refactored to the shared helper.
- Settings UI (Domain tab): fixed the A-record target (was a hardcoded wrong IP 72.62.69.9) to config \`DOMAIN_TARGET_IP\` = 51.79.226.215 + CNAME option (\`app.studionexis.com\`), shows all 4 states + FAILED reason, and a **Verify now** button.
- In-app DNS verify \`POST /api/settings/domain/verify\` (node:dns): confirms the domain resolves to this server before provisioning; PENDING/VERIFYING/FAILED.
- Root-free cron \`POST /api/cron/domains?token=CRON_TOKEN\`: promotes PENDING->VERIFYING and demotes LIVE->FAILED (a live domain that stops pointing here falls back to the subdomain immediately).
- Operator provisioner \`scripts/domain-provisioner.sh\` (root): Let's Encrypt cert via webroot, writes nginx vhost proxying the domain to 127.0.0.1:3105, smoke-tests, flips LIVE; re-checks live domains; cleans up removed ones.
- Renewal: existing \`certbot.timer\` + deploy hook \`scripts/nexis-cert-renew-hook.sh\` (reloads nginx after renewal).
- Prisma UNCHANGED (state lives in Tenant.policies JSON).

